CADMUS-CR-12  -  Secure Coding C/C++  -  V1, the Linux build host
==================================================================

You are on V1 ({{ cr12_ip_v1 }}). The application is POSIX C++ and its dynamic
analysis tier only exists on Linux, so it is built, run and analysed here.
You normally reach this machine from SC1 with VS Code (Remote-SSH: host "v1")
or with "ssh {{ cr12_trainee_user }}@v1" in a Windows terminal.

  Application            {{ cr12_app_dir }}
  Run it (loopback)      cd {{ cr12_app_dir }} && make && ./build/vulnshop config/sandbox.ini
                         VS Code forwards port {{ cr12_app_port }} to SC1 automatically:
                         http://localhost:{{ cr12_app_port }}/shop in the SC1 browser.
  Valgrind (Memcheck)    ~/lab-tools/valgrind-container.sh     -> lab/valgrind-report.txt
                         (natively:  ./tools/scan-valgrind.sh)
  Sanitizers, per request ~/lab-tools/replay-each.sh
  SonarQube analysis     ~/lab-tools/scan-sonar.sh -t <token>   (add -v to import Valgrind)
  Composition (Snyk)     snyk auth  (once), then  snyk test --unmanaged
  Environment check      ~/lab-tools/verify-v1.sh

  SonarQube              http://sq1:9000 from here, http://localhost:9000 on SC1

Notes
-----
* SonarQube Community Build has no C/C++ analyser of its own; this sandbox uses
  the community plugin sonar-cxx, which imports cppcheck (and Valgrind)
  reports. scan-sonar.sh does that for you. tools/scan-sonar.ps1 in the
  repository is for the commercial C/C++ analyser and does not apply here.
* The request corpus contains an oversized search query that crashes the
  service (finding M7). Everything after it in a single run is not observed -
  replay-each.sh gives every request its own process.
* When you commit in level D1, add the files you changed by name
  (git add src/...). Reports in lab/ and reports/ are not part of the fix.
* The application stays on 127.0.0.1. Do not change the bind address.
